# 🔤 FIGlet Text Generator (ASCII Art)

## 📌 Description
This Python program converts normal text into large stylized ASCII art using different fonts.

It is based on the classic FIGlet program and uses the `pyfiglet` library to render text in visually appealing formats directly in the terminal.

---

## 🎯 Objective
- Learn how to use third-party Python libraries
- Work with command-line arguments (`sys.argv`)
- Implement input validation and error handling
- Use randomness to enhance program functionality

---

## 🛠️ Technologies Used
- Python 3
- pyfiglet (third-party package)

---

## 📦 Installation

Install the required package using pip:

```bash
pip install pyfiglet


🚀 How to Run
▶️ Random Font
python figlet.py
▶️ Specific Font
python figlet.py -f slant

or

python figlet.py --font slant
💡 How It Works
The program checks command-line arguments:
No arguments → selects a random font
Two arguments → uses a specific font
If arguments are invalid, the program exits with an error message
The user inputs text
The program outputs the text in a stylized ASCII font
🧪 Example
Input:
Hello
Output:
 _   _      _
| | | | ___| | ___
| |_| |/ _ \ |/ _ \
|  _  |  __/ | (_) |
|_| |_|\___|_|\___/
⚠️ Error Handling

The program handles:

Invalid number of arguments
Incorrect flags (only -f or --font allowed)
Invalid font names
